Code delta: src/alg.rs installs a private owning guard immediately after successful
native open on both feature paths. Transfer disarms it once; error or unwinding
attempts one matching native close. Explicit property-error cleanup preserves the
primary failure and any close failure without retry. Gated wrappers observe the
same native open/property/provider-close calls; ledger ambiguity never vetoes the
provider close. src/lib.rs reexports the safe probe module; src/alg/probe.rs retains
the saved snapshot, distinct fixture recovery and cleanup-gap regression outcome.
No cached-initializer, ShutdownHandle, concurrency or provider-adoption fix is made.
The redundant parentheses around dyn ActiveKeyExchange in src/kx.rs are removed
for a warning-clean local-path build; the trait object and operation are unchanged.
Its imports also follow the caller's pinned formatter configuration.

TLS 1.2 descriptor correction: src/tls12.rs binds
TLS_ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 to AES_256_GCM (32-byte keys),
instead of the upstream AES_128_GCM (16-byte keys), as required by RFC 5289
section 3.2. src/tls12/tests.rs retains descriptor/key-block-shape regressions
and AES-128/RSA/TLS-1.3 neighbors for a later admitted provider test lane.
The Linux source-only checks in ../../tests/test_cipher_suite_mappings.py
exercise advertised identity -> AEAD binding -> declared key size, with faulty
binding/key-size controls. They execute no Rust or Windows CNG operation.
The held lifecycle fixture keeps provider defaults/TLS 1.2 disabled; no feature,
dependency, native-execution or product/provider-adoption gate is changed.

